<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Boral fined A$70,000 for gas leak.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Boral fined A$70,000 for gas leak.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boral Gas, a unit of building materials and energy group Boral Ltd, has been fined A$70,000 following the escape of liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) at its Port Botany plant in Sydney.</p>
<p>New South Wales state government attorney-general Jeff Shaw said in a statement that Boral Gas had been prosecuted under the Occupational Health and Safety Act for failing to ensure the health and safety of employees after the escape of LPG during an unloading operation in June 1991.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
